1. **`shell: true` Context**: Total.js internally uses `child_process.spawn()` with the `{ shell: true }` option to invoke external image processors (`gm`, `im`, or `magick`). When this option is enabled, Node.js passes the command string directly to `/bin/sh -c`. This means the operating system's shell parser will interpret all metacharacters (`, `, `;`, `"`, `` ` ``, etc.) instead of treating them as literal strings.

