   The first single quote breaks out of the format argument boundary. `';` ends the intended command. `/usr/bin/genpoc` executes with root/process privileges. `#` safely comments out the trailing syntax that would otherwise cause a shell parse error and abort execution.

3. **Verification & Patch Alignment**: 
