1. **Quantified Alternation Ambiguity**: The legacy regex `/^(?:\r|\n)+|(?:\r|\n)+$/g` uses `(?:\r|\n)+`. Inside a greedy `+`, each character position can legally be matched as either `\r` or `\n`. This creates exponential ambiguity when the match fails to extend further.
