2.  **Backtracking Explosion**: The engine tries to satisfy the greedy quantifiers (`\s*`, `[ \t]*`, etc.) in multiple ways as it fails to match digits deeper in the string. This results in **exponential time complexity** (or at least O(n²)), where execution time grows rapidly with input length.
