1. **Mechanism of Backtracking**: The vulnerable regex `/^(?:\r|\n)+|(?:\r|\n)+$/g` tells the engine to match either leading OR trailing sequences of `\r`/`\n`. When fed a string like `5000 × \r + \n + x`, the greedy `(?:\r|\n)+` consumes characters until it hits `x`. Because `x` doesn't satisfy `$` (end-of-string) and doesn't match `\r|\n`, the engine must backtrack. Due to the alternation `|`, V8's NFA repeatedly explores conflicting paths trying to partition the newline sequence between the leading and trailing matches, causing exponential time complexity `O(2^n)`.

